The task:
=============================================================
Build a generative model, e.g. a VAE, that can encode an image (x) to a learned latent representation, z or q(z).

We want this latent representation to be invariant to small transformations (small rotations (+/-10 degrees), scales (+/- 20%) and translations (+/- 4 pixels) i.e. q(z|x) = q(z|T(x)).

The accompanying latent space should be appropriate for classification using a simple linear classifier, and the classification accuracy should be evaluated.

The data:
=============================================================
Either Fashion MNIST or MNIST is fine, MedMNISTLinks to an external site. could also be an option or CIFAR.

What to hand in:
A 3 page (+ refs) report, and associated code that includes:

A diagram/psuedocode explaining how the model processes data.
plots of appropriate evaluation metrics.

Some investigation of the effects of architectures, losses and components with ablation studies and suitable baselines.

An investigation of model errors and common mistakes

A list of references
